From c8081586061f62855b791de8a8d96af26a22de85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xun2202 <98207886+Xun2202@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:15:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] updater: check this fork's GitHub releases for
 -harmony-preview builds

The stock updater asks api.github.com for mihonapp/mihon's latest release
and only understands v0.1.2 / r1234 version strings, so a build versioned
0.20.4-harmony.1 either crashes the parser or is offered the official APK,
which cannot be installed over an APK signed with a different key.

- AppUpdateChecker: GITHUB_REPO is Xun2202/mihon-harmony; RELEASE_TAG is
  derived from VERSION_NAME as v<ver>-harmony-preview.<N> (used by the
  "About" screen link).
- ReleaseServiceImpl: list /releases?per_page=30 and pick the newest tag
  containing "-harmony-preview." for preview builds, or "-harmony." without
  "preview" for release builds. ABI-based APK selection is unchanged, so
  release assets must keep the -arm64-v8a / -universal name fragments.
- GetApplicationRelease: compare (major, minor, patch, harmony) tuples
  parsed from "(\d+)\.(\d+)\.(\d+)-harmony(?:-preview)?\.(\d+)"; fall back to
  the upstream logic only when parsing fails, with toIntOrNull() so an
  unexpected tag cannot crash the app.
